From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:48:02 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: reset queue_ptr when preparing a
 stream

snd_pcm_prepare() rewinds appl_ptr, and the stale queue_ptr made the
unsigned (appl_ptr - queue_ptr) in q6asm_dai_ack() wrap around after a
re-prepare.

On 6.19 this patch also closed a stopped stream before opening it again.
Mainline does that since cee3e63e71, "ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: do not set
stream state in event and trigger callbacks".

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
index 4f09fdd409..d2f415e930 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
@@ -222,6 +222,7 @@ static int q6asm_dai_prepare(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	}
 
 	prtd->pcm_count = snd_pcm_lib_period_bytes(substream);
+	prtd->queue_ptr = 0;
 	/* rate and channels are sent to audio driver */
 	if (prtd->state == Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING) {
 		/* clear the previous setup if any  */
